# zidecar deployment

## single node (personal)

    zidecar --zebrad-rpc http://127.0.0.1:8232

## single node with caddy (public)

    ZIDECAR_DOMAIN=zcash.example.com caddy run --config Caddyfile.zidecar

## HA pair

    DNS A records → caddy-01 IP, caddy-02 IP

    on each caddy node:

    ZIDECAR_DOMAIN=zcash.example.com \
    ZIDECAR_BACKENDS="zidecar-01:50051 zidecar-02:50051" \
    caddy run --config Caddyfile.zidecar

    on each zidecar node:

    zidecar --zebrad-rpc http://local-zebrad:8232 \
            --listen 0.0.0.0:50051 \
            --mempool-cache-ttl 3

## zclid (wallet daemon)

    # start daemon — unix socket at ~/.zcli/zclid.sock, no auth (the
    # filesystem already answers who you are)
    zclid --endpoint https://zcash.rotko.net

    # add a TCP listener for remote callers (zafu, agents). Off unless asked
    # for; when on it requires `authorization: bearer <token>` against the
    # 256-bit token generated at ~/.zcli/zclid.token on first run.
    zclid --endpoint https://zcash.rotko.net --listen 127.0.0.1:9067

Clients speak the `WalletDaemon` gRPC service in bin/zclid/proto/zclid.proto:
GetBalance, GetNotes, GetStatus, GetAddress, GetHistory, GetPendingActivity,
GetCustodyMode, PrepareTransaction, SignAndSend, SubmitSigned,
SendRawTransaction.

NOTE: `zcli` itself does not talk to zclid yet — there is no client for it in
bin/zcli. `zcli view balance` still syncs on its own. zclid is consumed over
gRPC by zafu and by agents; wiring the CLI through it is not done.

## systemd

    cp zidecar.service /etc/systemd/system/
    cp zclid.service /etc/systemd/user/
    systemctl enable --now zidecar
    systemctl --user enable --now zclid
